{
    "background_story": "Liv was a free-spirited artist who found inspiration in the works of Mother Teresa. She had always been drawn to the selfless nun's compassion and dedication to helping others. As a tribute, Liv created a series of paintings depicting Mother Teresa's life and legacy. Her art gained international recognition, but Liv felt unfulfilled, yearning to make a more tangible impact. She began volunteering at local soup kitchens and eventually founded her own charity, providing art therapy to underprivileged children. Liv's organization, 'Teresa's Canvas,' flourished, bringing hope and creativity to those who needed it most. Through her art and philanthropy, Liv continued Mother Teresa's legacy, spreading love and kindness to all those she touched.",
